    "9. [Results and Interpretation](#results-and-interpretation)\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Project Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook presents a comprehensive analysis of bacterial strain classification using Raman spectroscopy data, specifically focusing on binary classification between **Penicillin** and **Meropenem** resistance patterns. The study employs a permutation test methodology to validate the statistical significance of the classification performance.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Objectives:\n",
    "- **Statistical Validation**: Use permutation testing to ensure the model's performance is statistically significant\n",
    "- **Methodology**: Apply strain-level permutation to maintain biological relevance while testing null hypotheses\n",
    "\n",
    "### Research Context:\n",
    "This work builds upon the methodology described in:\n",
    "- **Paper**: [Raman spectroscopy for bacterial identification](https://pubs.rsc.org/en/content/articlepdf/2022/ra/d2ra03722j)\n",
    "- **Dataset Source**: [Bacteria-ID GitHub Repository](https://github.com/csho33/bacteria-ID/blob/master/datasets.py)\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Dataset Description\n",
    "\n",
    "### Data Structure Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "The dataset consists of Raman spectroscopy measurements from bacterial strains with the following hierarchical structure:\n",
    "\n",
    "#### **Strain/Isolate Level (IDs 0-29)**\n",
    "- **Definition**: Fixed genetic identity representing one reference strain per organism/variant\n",
    "- **Storage**: Strain IDs stored as integers 0-29 in `y_*.npy` files\n",
    "- **Total Strains**: 30 different bacterial strains\n",
    "\n",
    "#### **Batch/Culture Level**\n",
    "Three independent regrowths of the same strain under different conditions:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Batch Type | Purpose | Sample Size | Description |\n",
    "|------------|---------|-------------|-------------|\n",
    "| **Reference** | Training | ~2000 spectra/strain | Large batch for model training |\n",
    "| **Finetune** | Optional adaptation | ~100 spectra/strain | Small batch for fine-tuning (not used) |\n",
    "| **Test** | Evaluation | ~100 spectra/strain | Held-out batch for final evaluation |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Important Note**: These represent separate culture/preparation events with different:\n",
    "- Day of preparation\n",
    "- Plate conditions  \n",
    "- Instrument settings\n",
    "- Environmental factors\n",
    "\n",
    "#### **Spectrum Level**\n",
    "- **Format**: 1000-dimensional vector per measurement\n",
    "- **Wavenumber Range**: ~381.98 to 1792.4 cm⁻¹\n",
    "- **Measurement Type**: Single-cell Raman spectroscopy\n",
    "- **Data Type**: Continuous intensity values\n",
    "\n",
    "### File Structure\n",
    "\n",
    "| File | Content | Shape | Purpose |\n",
    "|------|---------|-------|---------|\n",
    "| `X_reference.npy` | Reference spectra | (60000, 1000) | Training data |\n",
    "| `y_reference.npy` | Reference strain IDs | (60000,) | Training labels |\n",
    "| `X_test.npy` | Test spectra | (3000, 1000) | Evaluation data |\n",
    "| `y_test.npy` | Test strain IDs | (3000,) | Evaluation labels |\n",
    "| `wavenumbers.npy` | Raman axis values | (1000,) | Spectral coordinates |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Antibiotic Classification System\n",
    "\n",
    "**Important**: Antibiotic resistance labels are not directly stored in the `.npy` files. Instead, they are derived through a mapping system:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Strain ID** → **Antibiotic Class** (0-7) using `ATCC_GROUPINGS` from `config.py`\n",
    "- **Antibiotic Names** stored in `antibiotics` dictionary\n",
    "- **Binary Focus**: This study concentrates on classes 0 (Meropenem) and 5 (Penicillin)\n"
